problems.problem:
Let $GERMANYISHOT$ be a regular dodecagon. The lines $GN$ and $MI$ intersect at the point $P$. Prove that
(a) the circumcircle of triangle $GIP$ is as large as the circumcircle of $GERMANYISHOT$;
(b) the segment $PA$ is as long as a side of $GERMANYISHOT$.

Find all functions $f: \mathbb{R}_{>0} \times \mathbb{R}_{>0} \to \mathbb{R}_{>0}$ such that the following two conditions are satisfied:
(a) $f\left(f\left(\frac{x}{y}, y\right), z\right) = x \cdot f(1, z)$ for all $x, y, z \in \mathbb{R}_{>0}$;
(b) the function $g: \mathbb{R}_{>0} \to \mathbb{R}_{>0}$ defined by $g(x) = f(x, x)$ for all $x \in \mathbb{R}_{>0}$ is monotonic.
